      "message": "All,\n\nThis is the new software workaround to address https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/185308433.  I added some comments comparing the old workaround to this new one.\n\nI need some help from Google checking (and probably modifying) the code I implemented for the timeout.  The goal is to avoid sending the I2C command that actually writes register `LN9310_STARTUP_STANDBY_EN` to 0 if it has been longer than 100 ms since the previous I2C command (writing register `LN9310_LION_CTRL_MASK` to the value `LN9310_LION_CTRL_TEST_OFF_AND_UNLOCK`).  The way I have it written now is assuming `field_update8` can\u0027t be interrupted but I think that probably isn\u0027t true.  ",
